WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.190
Every autumn, streets in
Britain glow with Diwali lights.

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.720
Doorsteps fill with rows of small clay lamps
and bright patterns of coloured powder.

3
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:14.500
Then in spring, at the full moon,
people throw coloured powder and water,

4
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.640
young and old together.

5
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:20.310
Why lamps for one festival,
and colour for the other?

6
00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.990
In this mission, you'll
follow the Ramayana,

7
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:28.320
an ancient epic, from a bow strung
at a royal court to a long exile.

8
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:33.200
Then you'll uncover the stories behind
the bonfire on the night before Holi.

9
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:37.970
Your mission: find out what the lamps of
Diwali and the colours of Holi mean to

10
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:38.770
Hindus.
